    "title": "Death investigation underway in southeast Fort Wayne - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Gracie Sherrow No media credit provided. ,\n54 minutes ago\nFORT WAYNE, Ind. (WANE) – A death investigation is being conducted by the Fort Wayne Police Department at an apartment building on the city’s southeast side.\nAccording to a press release from FWPD, First responders were dispatched to the 6100 block on Wednesday at around 8:35 p.m. for reports of an unconscious man behind an apartment building.\nUpon arrival, officers began CPR, but once medics arrived, the man was pronounced dead.\nDetective and Crime Scene personnel are on scene collecting evidence to determine how the man died.\nAnyone with information on the incident is asked to call the Fort Wayne Police Department at 260-427-1222, Crimestoppers, or use the P3 Tips App.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
    "summary": "(WANE) – A death investigation is being conducted by the Fort Wayne Police Department at an apartment building on the city’s southeast side. According to a press release from FWPD, First responders were dispatched to the 6100 block on Wednesday at around 8:35 p.m. for reports of an unconscious man behind an apartment building. Anyone with information on the incident is asked to call the Fort Wayne Police Department at 260-427-1222, Crimestoppers, or use the P3 Tips App. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.",
